      ],
      "shortDescription": "Hyderabad's 16th-century four-minaret monument, at the centre of the old city's bustling bazaars.",
      "description": "The Charminar's four 56 m minarets rise above a square arch structure at the heart of Hyderabad's old city. A narrow staircase leads to an upper floor with a small mosque and views over the surrounding bazaars. Laad Bazaar, famous for lacquer bangles, runs west from its base, and the great Mecca Masjid is next door. The monument is lit up in the evenings, and the area is busiest during Ramzan nights.",
      "history": "Sultan Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah built the Charminar in 1591 when he founded Hyderabad, possibly to mark the end of a plague. It is a protected monument of the Archaeological Survey of India.",
      "bestMonths": [
        10,
