    {
      "name": "Golconda Fort",
      "slug": "golconda-fort",
      "city": "hyderabad",
      "kind": "fort",
      "categories": [
        "heritage",
        "adventure"
      ],
      "shortDescription": "A hilltop citadel of the Qutb Shahi kings, famed for its acoustics, water systems and diamond trade.",
      "description": "Golconda Fort spreads over a granite hill on Hyderabad's western edge, enclosed by massive walls and gateways. A clap under the dome of the Fateh Darwaza entrance can be heard at the Bala Hissar pavilion at the summit, a clever early alarm system. The climb to the top passes granaries, palaces, mosques and water channels, and rewards with views over the city. The evening sound-and-light show retells the fort's history; the Qutb Shahi tombs are nearby.",
      "history": "A mud fort built by the Kakatiyas was rebuilt in stone by the Qutb Shahi sultans, who made Golconda their capital from 1518 until the Mughal emperor Aurangzeb captured it in 1687 after a long siege. The region was famous for diamonds such as the Koh-i-Noor.",
      "bestMonths": [
        10,
