      ],
      "shortDescription": "A UNESCO-listed 13th-century Kakatiya temple, named after its sculptor and known for its floating bricks.",
      "description": "The Rudreshwara Temple at Palampet, better known as Ramappa after the sculptor who built it, is a masterpiece of Kakatiya art. Its pillars and brackets are carved from hard dolerite and granite with dancers, musicians and mythical beasts so finely detailed they almost seem metallic. The temple's tower is built of bricks so light they float on water. The nearby Ramappa lake, a Kakatiya-era reservoir, is still in use.",
      "history": "The temple was built in 1213 CE by Recharla Rudra, a general of the Kakatiya king Ganapati Deva. It was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2021.",
